#: src/std-types/std.md:6
msgid "Standard Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/std-types/std.md:8
msgid ""
"Rust comes with a standard library that helps establish a set of common "
"types used by Rust libraries and programs. This way, two libraries can work "
"together smoothly because they both use the same `String` type."
msgstr ""

#: src/std-types/std.md:12
msgid ""
"In fact, Rust contains several layers of the Standard Library: `core`, "
"`alloc` and `std`."
msgstr ""

#: src/std-types/std.md:15
msgid ""
"`core` includes the most basic types and functions that don't depend on "
"`libc`, allocator or even the presence of an operating system."
msgstr ""

#: src/std-types/std.md:17
msgid ""
"`alloc` includes types that require a global heap allocator, such as `Vec`, "
"`Box` and `Arc`."
msgstr ""

#: src/std-types/std.md:19
msgid ""
"Embedded Rust applications typically only use `core`, and sometimes `alloc`."
msgstr ""
